		<item>
		<title>MITB Cash In with big title change takes place at Crown Jewel on Saturday</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396911-mitb-cash-in-with-big-title-change-takes-place-at-crown-jewel-on-saturday/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396911-mitb-cash-in-with-big-title-change-takes-place-at-crown-jewel-on-saturday/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 19:13:35 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[cash in]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Chelsea Green]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Crown Jewel]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Tiffany Stratton]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Women's Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=396911</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Tiffany Stratton turned heel and cashed in her Money in the Bank briefcase on Chelsea Green to win&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396911-mitb-cash-in-with-big-title-change-takes-place-at-crown-jewel-on-saturday/">MITB Cash In with big title change takes place at Crown Jewel on Saturday</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tiffany Stratton turned heel and cashed in her Money in the Bank briefcase on Chelsea Green to win the Women&#8217;s Championship, at <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/396823-wwe-crown-jewel-results-11-7-26-mens-and-womens-crown-jewel-championships-and-more/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Crown Jewel</a> in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia on Saturday. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Green defeated Liv Morgan to win the Women&#8217;s Crown Jewel Championship.  While giving a speech in the ring, after celebrating, Morgan blindsided Green.  Out came Tiffany Stratton with her Money in the Bank briefcase. Stratton tells the referee she wants to cash in. However, Raquel Rodriguez and Roxanne Perez come down to cause interference, but were fended off by Green. As Green turns around, Stratton whacked Green with the briefcase. Stratton cashes in, hits the Prettiest Moonsault Ever on Green to get the pin.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">What a moment for <a href="https://x.com/ImChelseaGreen?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">@ImChelseaGreen</a>! <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f44f.png" alt="👏" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <a href="https://t.co/meHkYA6i8p">pic.twitter.com/meHkYA6i8p</a></p>&mdash; WWE (@WWE) <a href="https://x.com/WWE/status/2119140591221006371?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">NO WAY!!!<br><br>Some kind of friend you are, <a href="https://x.com/tiffstrattonwwe?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">@tiffstrattonwwe</a> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f621.png" alt="😡" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <a href="https://t.co/64L3AlEgEl">pic.twitter.com/64L3AlEgEl</a></p>&mdash; WWE (@WWE) <a href="https://x.com/WWE/status/2119141643714466295?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396911-mitb-cash-in-with-big-title-change-takes-place-at-crown-jewel-on-saturday/">MITB Cash In with big title change takes place at Crown Jewel on Saturday</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396911-mitb-cash-in-with-big-title-change-takes-place-at-crown-jewel-on-saturday/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>WWE Crown Jewel Results – 11/7/26 (Men&#8217;s and Women&#8217;s Crown Jewel Championships and more!)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396823-wwe-crown-jewel-results-11-7-26-mens-and-womens-crown-jewel-championships-and-more/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396823-wwe-crown-jewel-results-11-7-26-mens-and-womens-crown-jewel-championships-and-more/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE Crown Jewel Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/7/26 WWE Crown Jewel results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Crown Jewel Championship]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Last Man Standing]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[World Tag Team Championship]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=396823</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>WWE Crown Jewel ResultsNovember 7, 2026Riyadh, Saudi Arabia (ANB Arena)Results by: Alex Kahrs of Wrestleview.com WWE: Then. Now.&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396823-wwe-crown-jewel-results-11-7-26-mens-and-womens-crown-jewel-championships-and-more/">WWE Crown Jewel Results – 11/7/26 (Men&#8217;s and Women&#8217;s Crown Jewel Championships and more!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>WWE Crown Jewel Results</strong><br><strong>November 7, 2026</strong><br><strong>Riyadh, Saudi Arabia (ANB Arena)</strong><br><strong>Results by: Alex Kahrs of Wrestleview.com</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em><strong>WWE: Then. Now. Forever. Together.</strong></em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Commentary (wherever they may be) welcomes us to the show, where we see an excited crowd before going to the arrival of the Crown Jewel Championships, as well as Superstar Arrivals for the main players going into the show tonight (I say, taking a bite out of my Wheaties). We then go to a video hyping up the show itself, focused on the Crown Jewel Championship matches.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We head back to ringside, where Cody Rhodes makes his entrance for our opening contest, the crowd singing along with his theme on his way down the ramp. Commentary talks up the importance of this match for Rhodes as he enters the ring. Out next is Randy Orton, and the crowd switches up to sing along with HIS theme as he makes his entrance. We get the occasional shot of Cody staring down his former pal from the ring as Orton has quite time with the crowd reaction on his way down the ramp.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Randy&#8217;s music loops back around as he enters the ring, still soaking in the adulation of the crowd as he poses. They are still singing along as the bell rings to get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="last-man-standing-match-cody-rhodes-vs-randy-orton" class="wp-block-heading">Last Man Standing Match: Cody Rhodes vs. Randy Orton</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">No time for a lock up, as Orton sends Cody to the corner. Rhodes starts to fight back before being sent across the ring&#8230;where he dodges a shoulder tackle, forcing Orton to collide with the ring post. Ref begins the count, until Orton falls to the floor on his feet. Cody goes right back after him, and the two fight it out until Cody gets slammed against the announce table.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He falls to the floor as the ref begins the count, but Rhodes is already back on his feet&#8230;only to be dropped onto the table once again by Orton, who props up the cowl of the table before sending him through it. He tells the ref to make a count but Cody is able to get up around the count of four. Back on his feet, Cody takes Orton into the crowd&#8230;only to be fought off by the Viper, who grabs a nearby trashcan to slam against Cody&#8217;s head! Ref starts the count but Cody is back up quick, before Orton slams him in the head with the lid of the trashcan. Another count reaches about five when Cody gets back up&#8230;and Randy hits him with the lid again.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cody fights back some more, sending Orton over the barricade and back to ringside. He is afforded a quick hydration break before getting back to ringside himself&#8230;where Randy awaits with a kendo stick! Cody tries to get away by getting back in the ring, but Orton continues the attack until Rhodes is able to grab the stick and fight back. Randy is forced out of the ring, landing on the apron on his way down as the ref comes out to start the count. He reaches seven when Orton manages to get to his feet, but Cody blindsides him to start a new count from the referee. Orton back up at five, as Cody follows him up the ramp, eventually sending him into the LED screen on the stage.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ref begins the count anew as Cody disappears to the back&#8230;before returning with a trashcan of his own, attacking the Viper to send him to the stage once again. New count is stopped when Orton gets to his feet, and we see Cody return from the back with a table this time. He grabs the trashcan and slams it against Orton&#8230;who answers with a right hand, sending Cody toward the table.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He sets the American Nightmare up for a fall, driving him through the table with a powerbomb. Ref count reaches eight before Cody gets to his feet. Orton doesn&#8217;t give him much breathing room, going to work on him down the ramp toward the ring. He sends Rhodes back into the ring, favoring his shoulder as he gets to the apron&#8230;where Cody intercepts him for a draping DDT from the second rope!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">New count begins as Cody goes up top, looking to do more damage when Orton gets back on his feet&#8230;but Randy goes to the ropes, dropping Rhodes onto his little American Nightmares instead! Randy lands some shots on Cody, followed by a lowkey throwback to his dad Bob Orton with a superplex dropping Cody to the canvas! Cody back on his feet already but gets dropped again by Orton&#8230;who follows up with a draping DDT of his own! Cody slowly gets to his feet to break the count at five, but Randy is setting up for an RKO.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cody gets away from it, hitting the ropes for some offense before dropping Orton with a powerslam. Cody Cutter from the middle rope keeps Orton down for a count of seven. Cody goes after him with some punches, looking for a Bionic Elbow like his old man Dusty&#8230;only to be dropped with an RKO out of nowhere by Orton! Cody manages to get up at eight, rolling out of the way of Orton to get to the outside.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Orton pulls the ring steps apart, hoisting up the top half to slam against Rhodes while he&#8217;s propped against the ring post&#8230;but Cody narrowly dodges it, using the step on Orton instead! Ref starts a new count, but Cody goes right back on the attack. He sets Randy up on the announce table before looking for a weapon under the ring&#8230;deciding on a ladder that he sets up near the table!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He lands some shots on Orton to keep him on the table before making his ascent up the ladder&#8230;but just as he leaps off the ladder, Randy rolls out of the way with Cody sending himself through the table! Both men are down as the ref begins the count. Orton back up at eight, and Rhodes narrowly back up at nine.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The action finds its way back to the ring now, where Cody struggles to get to his feet. The ref sees this as the need to start a new count, but Cody practically begs the ref off as he gets back up enough to break the count. Randy sees his opening and goes for a punt&#8230;but Cody dodges it at the last second, landing a super Cody Cutter to take Orton to the mat!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ref with a new count, but Orton is back up at eight&#8230;just as Cody grabs him for a Cross Rhodes! New count begins as Cody stares down Orton before leaving the ring. The count reaches nine for Randy before he gets back up using the ropes. Meanwhile, Cody brings the ring step and a chair into the ring as he looks to do more damage. Chair to the gut and back of Orton, and a right hand by Cody puts the Viper on the ring step.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cody grabs the chair, staring Randy down as he stands over him with the chair lifted up&#8230;only for Orton to fire back with a low blow! Rhodes drops to the mat as the ref starts the count, and Cody is back up at eight. Orton goes after him, but gets caught with a Cross Rhodes not once but twice&#8230;and a third one for good measure to send Orton down hard. Ref starts a new count as Cody gets to his feet. Orton barely on his feet at the count of nine&#8230;and Cody stops the ref from counting any further!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He stares Orton down as he backs toward the corner&#8230;and connects with a punt to Randy&#8217;s head! He stares Orton down as the ref begins the count&#8230;and this one reaches ten! Randy is out cold and the ref calls for the bell to bring this match to an end.</p>



<h3 id="winner-last-man-standing-cody-rhodes" class="wp-block-heading">Winner (Last Man Standing): Cody Rhodes</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Cody Rhodes is the Last Man Standing to kick off <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a> <a href="https://t.co/L6ZRkWAZPi">pic.twitter.com/L6ZRkWAZPi</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119123183882412446?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Strong opening match to kick off <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a> between Cody Rhodes and Randy Orton. Really good culmination of the feud they&#39;ve been having, w/ the big moment of Rhodes following thru on landing the punt on Orton.</p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119123463684415746?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Curiously mixed reaction to the result here, and even Cody seems not quite himself (perhaps over having to resort to the punt?) as he leaves the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We go to a look back at Raw on Monday, with the 946 attacking the Bloodline during the main event and Sami Zayn taking advantage of the damage done to Roman Reigns. They face off tonight with the Crown Jewel Championship on the line.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Up next, the World Tag Team Championship is on the line as The Vision of Bron Breakker and Austin Theory defend against Penta and Je&#8217;Von Evans!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After a quick pitch for the upcoming Royal Rumble we head back to ringside, as Je&#8217;Von Evans makes his entrance for our next match to a nice reaction from the crowd. Penta comes out to the ring next, holding his Money in the Bank briefcase (with pyro and everything!), the fans loving him as he heads down the ramp. Commentary brings up the fact he&#8217;s in the same building as the World Heavyweight Champion and the Undisputed WWE Champion on a night they face off, as Penta gets into the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With that, The Vision makes their entrance. Maxxine accompanies the tag champs on their way to the ring, where they pose with the tag titles before we get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="world-tag-team-championship-the-vision-bron-breakker-and-austin-theory-defend-against-penta-and-jevon-evans" class="wp-block-heading">World Tag Team Championship: The Vision (Bron Breakker and Austin Theory) defend against Penta and Je’Von Evans</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Je&#8217;Von and Theory starting things off as they lock up, with Austin taking Evans to the corner. He fires off some shots until the ref intervenes. Maxxine urges her man on as Theory sends Evans across the ring, but Je&#8217;Von fires back with some shots of his own! Tag to Penta as the challengers take the fight to Austin, sending him out of the ring. Bron comes in but is sent to the outside alongside Theory, and Penta and Evans dive through the ropes sending the champs to the floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Theory brought back into the ring, where Penta gets him with a Backstabber from the corner. Evans lands a big frog splash on Austin for a two count. Theory brings Evans out of the ring, sending him crashing into a camera and then the barricade. Theory goes back to work on Penta, tying his mask to the ropes for a moment before tagging in Breakker&#8230;who drops Penta to the mat for a nearfall. He sends the luchador into the corner, where he lands some more shots before Penta fires back with a cross body for two.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bron with a big right hand takes Penta down for a nearfall once more, going for a chinlock after. Penta struggles to break free, getting to his feet for some right hands and a thrust kick twice over. He goes to the ropes but Breakker gets him with a German suplex.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tag made to Theory for a double team, and Austin gets a two count before knocking Evans off the apron. He goes back to work on Penta, enjoying the hate the crowd is giving him before tagging Breakker back in. The Vision with a beatdown, before Breakker takes Penta to the mat with a belly to belly suplex. This sends Penta to the corner as Breakker looks for a spear&#8230;and runs into a superkick!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tag made to Je&#8217;Von as Theory tags in as well, but Austin is sent to the corner where Evans connects with an OG Cutter to a big pop from the crowd. He knocks Breakker off the apron before going for a Red Dot&#8230;but Theory catches him with a rack bomb for two instead! Breakker comes back in with a tag, but is fended off by Evans, who looks for a tag but Penta is still down. This allows Breakker to take him down hard for a nearfall. Down go the straps as Breakker gears up for a spear&#8230;running into a kick by Je&#8217;Von instead, who sends Theory back to the outside before making the tag to Penta!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Penta sends Breakker to the corner with a sling blade, and Evans gets a tag back in for a nearfall. Theory breaks the pin, garnering a &#8220;f&#8211;k you Austin&#8221; chant as he goes for a DDT&#8230;but Evans kicks out before making the tag to Penta! Penta takes Theory down for a cover, but Maxxine gets his foot on the rope to break the count. In the midst of all this, Bronson Reed comes through the crowd, pulling Penta out of the ring to land a Death Valley Driver on him to the floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He clotheslines Evans over the barricade before running away. Penta is brought back in the ring for a Doomsday Device by The Vision, but it&#8217;s only good for two! Reed is still hanging around at ringside as Oba Femi&#8217;s music hits, bringing out The Ruler. Reed goes after him up the ramp, but is sent through a table off the stage by Oba. Bron has a staredown with the fellow hoss from ringside, as Evans tries to go for a dive to no avail&#8230;but Penta connects with one from the top turnbuckle!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He goes after Theory back in the ring for a Mexican Destroyer, and Evans follows up with an OG Cutter for the win! We have new champs!</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-pinfall-and-new-world-tag-team-champions-penta-and-jevon-evans" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via pinfall and new World Tag Team Champions: Penta and Je&#8217;Von Evans</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Je&#39;Von Evans and Penta are your NEW World Tag Team Champions at <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a> <a href="https://t.co/bBYEICVhwT">pic.twitter.com/bBYEICVhwT</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119131985809649705?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Almost surprisingly good World Tag Title match here at <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a> &#8230; the match briefly felt more at home on Raw, but even with the involvement of Bronson Reed and Oba Femi this turned out to be a fun time had. New champs, to top it all off!</p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119132759704936781?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We get a replay of the chaos going on during the match leading to the finish, as the new champs celebrate.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We get a look backstage at the men&#8217;s and women&#8217;s Crown Jewel Championships, with the first of these matches coming up next!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After some hype for WWE going to Perth in December we get a video package hyping up the women&#8217;s Crown Jewel Championship match, with Liv Morgan taking on Chelsea Green!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, we get a look at the women&#8217;s Crown Jewel Championship on display in the ring as Liv Morgan makes her entrance first. She gives the title she won previously a look before posing on the ropes as a notable section of the crowd sings along with her theme. Out next is Chelsea Green, also getting a strong reaction from the crowd as she heads to the ring. We get ring introductions for both champions, and with that we get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="womens-crown-jewel-championship-wwe-womens-world-champion-liv-morgan-vs-wwe-womens-champion-chelsea-green" class="wp-block-heading">Women’s Crown Jewel Championship: WWE Women’s World Champion Liv Morgan vs. WWE Women’s Champion Chelsea Green</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Smattering of a &#8220;Chelsea&#8221; chant as the two women lock up. Morgan takes Green to the mat and has a dance over it. Chelsea goes after Morgan, but gets sent back down for her efforts. Liv mocks her fellow champion to a &#8220;You suck&#8221; chant, before Green gets a roll up on her for two. Liv hits the ropes for a basement dropkick, as we get a &#8220;Chelsea, Chelsea Green&#8221; chant. Liv offers her a hand to get up&#8230;only to knock her back down.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Green has had enough as she fires off some hip tosses on the Women&#8217;s World Champion, forcing her to the outside. Liv eventually comes back in, cutting off a dive with a clothesline. She takes Green to the ropes, continuing the attack with another dropkick sending Chelsea to the ropes. Chelsea back up with a boot to Morgan, but Liv takes the WWE Women&#8217;s Champion down with a Codebreaker for a nearfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">She sends Green into the ring post for further damage, going for a half crab in the ropes before taking Chelsea to the mat with a bulldog for two. She continues the attack before cinching in a chinlock. Green starts to fight back but is pulled to the canvas by Morgan.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Liv with a suplex on Chelsea, and she completes the Three Amigos. Chelsea starts to get up but is taken back down with a kick by Morgan, who heads up top only to be intercepted by Green. They fight it out on the turnbuckle with Chelsea knocked back&#8230;only to catch Liv with a superplex!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Chelsea&#8217;s offense is quickly shuttered by the Women&#8217;s World Champion, who takes Green to the mat for a two count. Chelsea uses the ropes to get back up, blocking an Oblivion attempt before going for a Rough Ryder&#8230;but Morgan counters, stacking her up for a nearfall instead. Liv goes for an Unpretty-Her&#8230;but Green counters out, looking for one of her own. She&#8217;s sent to the ropes by Morgan&#8230;only to bounce back with a Rough Ryder! Cover by Chelsea, but it&#8217;s only good for a nearfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Green has Morgan on the ropes, but Liv counters with another Codebreaker for two. She quickly transitions to a half crab, as Chelsea crawls toward the ropes. Liv pulls her back to the center, keeping a tight grip on the leg of Green&#8230;who manages to get to the ropes the second time around for the break! Liv stomps away at the WWE Women&#8217;s Champion before heading to the turnbuckle. Off the second rope she goes for&#8230;well, nothing, as she takes a thrust kick to the face by Chelsea!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Green back to her feet as Morgan escapes to the outside, only to be taken to the floor with a dive by Chelsea. She gets back in the ring as Liv gets back up&#8230;but to no avail as Green takes her out with another dive! She brings Liv back in the ring for a missile dropkick. Unpretty-Her is blocked, but so is Oblivion as Green connects with the Unpretty-Her&#8230;but it only gets a two when Liv gets her foot on the bottom rope.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Morgan is still down as Chelsea goes up top&#8230;but Roxanne Perez and Raquel Rodriguez come out for a distraction. Liv sends Green to the outside, leaving the ring as she asks her pals what they&#8217;re doing out here. She says she&#8217;s got this and tells them to head back before she takes Green back to the ring. She goes for Oblivion&#8230;and Green counters with a flash pin for the win!</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-and-2026-womens-crown-jewel-champion-chelsea-green" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall and 2026 Women&#8217;s Crown Jewel Champion: Chelsea Green</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Chelsea Green is your 2026 Women&#39;s Crown Jewel Champion coming out of <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a> <a href="https://t.co/2jqVTJkmTJ">pic.twitter.com/2jqVTJkmTJ</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119140554898579954?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A surprised Green starts to celebrate with anyone she can at ringside, before returning to the ring where Triple H presents her with the Crown Jewel Championship title belt and ring. She is given a microphone for a speech, where she addresses thirteen years of being told she couldn&#8217;t make it&#8230;but she did it! She starts to tell us we can call her the greatest women&#8217;s champion of alllll ti&#8211;but Liv blindsides her!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Out comes Tiffany Stratton with her Money in the Bank briefcase! Liv&#8217;s face drops at the sight of her, and gets laid out as Tiffany tells the ref she wants to cash in. Judgment Day come out to interfere, but are fended off by Chelsea Green&#8230;who gets laid out by Tiffy with the briefcase! She&#8217;s turned her back on her best friend (for the second time!) as she reveals she&#8217;s cashing in on Green. The announcement is made&#8230;</p>



<h3 id="wwe-womens-championship-chelsea-green-defends-against-tiffany-stratton" class="wp-block-heading">WWE Women&#8217;s Championship: Chelsea Green defends against Tiffany Stratton</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8230;and Green never gets a chance to fight back as Tiffy hits the Prettiest Moonsault Ever as the ref slides into the ring. The bell sounds off just in time for the ref to make the count, and we have a new WWE Women&#8217;s Champion.</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-and-new-wwe-womens-champion-tiffany-stratton" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall and new WWE Women&#8217;s Champion: Tiffany Stratton</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Tiffany Stratton cashes in her Money in the Bank briefcase&#8230;and defeats Chelsea Green to become the NEW WWE Women&#39;s Champion at <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a> <a href="https://t.co/oLa1KWyAxG">pic.twitter.com/oLa1KWyAxG</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119142781864268022?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Tiffany takes the title she&#8217;s just won as well as the Crown Jewel Title and ring, celebrating on the ramp as we get some hype for the main event up next.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Ah, there it is. All the good vibes I was having about this show, gone in a flash. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119143118591365614?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">I enjoyed the women&#39;s Crown Jewel match a great deal, but we couldn&#39;t just have that feel good moment could we? Nah. We get a repeat of the Nia-Tiffy story, this time with Chelsea Green. Can&#39;t say I liked that, but I also get it. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119143273835229686?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We get a look at the different languages on display for commentary throughout the night. With that, we get a video package hyping out our main event for the men&#8217;s Crown Jewel Championship between Roman Reigns and Sami Zayn! We head back to ringside, where we get a look at the title these two men are competing for as Sami Zayn makes his entrance first. Crowd definitely still behind the Undisputed WWE Champion, singing to his theme and chanting his name&#8230;until Roman Reigns makes his entrance.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He makes his way down the ramp, posing with many in the crowd showing their acknowledgement of the World Heavyweight Champion as he makes his way to the ring. Roman poses with his title as he stares down Sami, and we get our ring introductions to get this main event underway!</p>



<h3 id="mens-crown-jewel-championship-wwe-world-heavyweight-champion-roman-reigns-vs-undisputed-wwe-champion-sami-zayn" class="wp-block-heading">Men’s Crown Jewel Championship: WWE World Heavyweight Champion Roman Reigns vs. Undisputed WWE Champion Sami Zayn</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sami tosses his hoodie at Roman, who has a laugh about it before tossing it to the outside. &#8220;Ole&#8221; chants for Sami as the two men circle the mat. Roman takes Zayn to the corner, but Sami turns it around as the ref intervenes for a break. Sami shoves Roman before backing off. &#8220;Sami, Sami Zayn&#8221; chants as the Undisputed WWE Champion goes for a side headlock&#8230;but Roman drives him toward the corner instead.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Roman is the one backing off now, before we get another side headlock from Sami. Roman sends him to the ropes for a shoulder tackle before firing off some more shots. Side headlock from Reigns this time, but Sami gets to the ropes and ends up sending the World Heavyweight Champion to the outside.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Roman starts to enter the ring but is sent back to the floor by Sami, who follows him closely to slam Reigns against the barricade. He keeps on the attack, which gets dangerously close to the Crown Jewel title and then the announce table&#8230;where Roman gets slammed face first! Sami brings him back into the ring, but Reigns fights back to get Zayn on the ropes.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sami uses the ropes to dodge Roman, taking him down for a nearfall. Sami fires off some more shots sending Roman to the corner. He goes to the second rope for a double ax handle and a nearfall, keeping Roman down for another close two count. Sami goes back up, but gets caught with a right hand by Reigns who takes control.  Clothesline off the ropes by Roman as Sami scrambles to the corner, only to be walloped with another flurry by Reigns before the Undisputed WWE Champion is sent to the canvas with a knee.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He brings Sami back to his feet, but Zayn starts to fight back before Roman drives him down with a suplex for a close nearfall. The crowd are trying to will Sami back into this, but Roman is having none of it as he drives Sami into the ropes before landing the drive-by kick. He gets back in the ring for a cover, but Sami manages to kick out. Sami with a right hand but is only met with another kick by Reigns.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We get a smattering of an OTC (or maybe it was Oba Femi, lol) chant with boos as Roman continues to go to work on Sami, taking him to the corner. Roman mocks those not in favor with him as he props Zayn up on the turnbuckle. He talks about going to superplex Sami&#8217;s &#8220;b&#8212;h a&#8211;&#8221; but Sami fights back with a sunset powerbomb for two! Roman with a couple elbow shots before countering the Blue Thunder Bomb with an uranage slam, sending Zayn down hard.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Roman heads to the corner for a Superman Punch, but Sami dodges it and counters with a Blue Thunder Bomb for a nearfall! Roman crawls to the corner, which gives Zayn the idea to go for a Helluva Kick. Roman dodges it, escaping to the outside&#8230;but the Undisputed WWE Champion catches him with a dive through the ropes, sending Reigns to the floor.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Roman is the first back in control as both men get to the ring, however, taking Sami down for a nearfall. Both men fight to their feet until Sami is sent to the corner for a clothesline. He runs back to the corner, narrowly dodging a Helluva Kick to take Zayn down with a Superman Punch. He sets up for a spear in the corner, only to be blindsided with a Helluva Kick! Cover by Sami&#8230;and Roman kicks out!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sami back in the corner as Roman gets back up. Sami goes for a Superman Punch but nearly collides with the ref instead&#8230;who gets knocked out with a Superman Punch by Reigns! No pin here as the ref is down, and this allows Sami to set Roman up for a Helluva Kick. He goes for the cover, and down comes Charles Robinson as a backup ref. He makes the count, and Roman kicks out just in time.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Robinson backs off to the corner as a frustrated Sami levels him with a Helluva Kick. At first, he seems to regret what he did&#8230;but then he heads to the outside to grab the Crown Jewel title. He brings it back to the ring, looking to use it&#8230;but gets laid out with a spear by Roman instead! Cover by Reigns as Chad Patton (the first ref) makes the count&#8230;only for Sami to kick out just in the nick of time.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Roman admits that he respects Sami&#8217;s effort, but it&#8217;s gonna take more than that to take the Tribal Chief down. He brings Sami to his feet as both men fight back and forth&#8230;and Reigns wins this battle, knocking Sami down with a right hand. Zayn is back on his feet, only to take another right hand sending him to the canvas.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Sami is back up again, telling Roman to give him everything he&#8217;s got&#8230;to which Roman responds with a Superman Punch. He goes for a spear, but gets trapped in an exploder by Zayn into the turnbuckle. He looks for a Helluva Kick but ends up taking a Superman Punch instead.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As he goes for a spear, Roman ends up getting hit with a Superman Punch by Zayn this time&#8230;only to take him out with a Superman Punch when Sami goes for a spear. Roman follows up with a spear, and it&#8217;s enough to keep Sami down for the three count!</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-and-2026-mens-crown-jewel-champion-roman-reigns" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall and 2026 Men&#8217;s Crown Jewel Champion: Roman Reigns</h3>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Roman Reigns is your 2026 Men&#39;s Crown Jewel Champion coming out of <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a> <a href="https://t.co/WRWypGGl4E">pic.twitter.com/WRWypGGl4E</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119153900758671555?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We get replays of the final moments of our main event as Roman starts to celebrate the win. Triple H arrives to present the title to Roman, but Sami tells him there&#8217;s something he needs from Reigns first. He goes to Roman, shouting at him that he deserves to get a handshake from Reigns. It took Roman everything he had to beat Sami, and he demands that Reigns admit that and shake his hand.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Roman slaps the hand away&#8230;choosing instead to hug the man once known as the Honorary Uce to a big pop from the crowd. Sami raises the arm of Reigns, who returns the favor for his fellow champion. Triple H hands Sami his WWE Title with a handshake, and Sami takes his leave with the respect he always wanted. Triple H presents Roman with the Crown Jewel Title and ring, as well as a microphone as Roman gives a speech saying there&#8217;s only one thing left to do. Kingdom of Saudi Arabia&#8230;acknowledge me!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Big pop from the crowd as Roman&#8217;s music hits, and we get some more pyro as he poses with the Crown Jewel Title to bring this show to a close.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Am I a fan of the result? Nah, but I&#39;ve been a Sami Zayn guy for a looong time. But the match itself? Really good. Bit of the usual drama you&#39;d expect, but rightfully deserved given the history between Zayn and Roman. <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a></p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119155884777755029?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">I will never pretend to be a fan of the circumstances behind <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a> even happening this year&#8230;but I mostly enjoyed the wrestling on display. We&#39;re in an era of WWE where the bar is set at &quot;better than a Raw or SmackDown&quot; and this managed to clear that bar.</p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119156737651671385?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">What did you think of the 2026 edition of <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/WWECrownJewel?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#WWECrownJewel</a> on 11/7?</p>&mdash; Wrestleview.com (@wrestleview) <a href="https://x.com/wrestleview/status/2119157752824230202?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 7, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<h3 id="quick-results" class="wp-block-heading">Quick Results:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Last Man Standing Match:</strong> Cody Rhodes def. Randy Orton</li>



<li><strong>World Tag Team Championship:</strong> Penta and Je’Von Evans def. The Vision (Bron Breakker and Austin Theory)</li>



<li><strong>Women’s Crown Jewel Championship:</strong> WWE Women’s Champion Chelsea Green def. WWE Women’s World Champion Liv Morgan</li>



<li><strong>WWE Women&#8217;s Championship:</strong> Tiffany Stratton def. Chelsea Green</li>



<li><strong>Men’s Crown Jewel Championship:</strong> WWE World Heavyweight Champion Roman Reigns def. Undisputed WWE Champion Sami Zayn</li>
</ul>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/396823-wwe-crown-jewel-results-11-7-26-mens-and-womens-crown-jewel-championships-and-more/">WWE Crown Jewel Results – 11/7/26 (Men&#8217;s and Women&#8217;s Crown Jewel Championships and more!)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
